<!-- Q&A -->
<section class="faq-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-label">Questions</div>
    <h2 class="section-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">Is this a full VR production crew?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">No. The proposed model is one embedded immersive storyteller working alongside the existing production team.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">Would this disrupt the main production?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">It shouldn't. The immersive capture focuses only on selected moments where 360° adds unique value, and would coordinate with the existing crew.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">What's the camera approach?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Lightweight 360° as the core (Insta360 Pro 2, X5, aerial), with premium stereoscopic capture possible for select scenes if logistics and budget allow.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">Where could people watch it?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Meta Quest TV, YouTube 360, Defender's own digital channels, headset-based dealer activations, motor shows, press rooms, internal JLR/Defender events, sponsor activations, a dedicated Defender Trophy immersive app, Reality Telling healthcare/elderly care deployments.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">Could it live in a dedicated app?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Yes. Reality Telling already has an app structure that could potentially be adapted into a Defender Trophy immersive catalog, allowing multiple experiences to live together instead of one single video.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">What would Defender get from this?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">An immersive archive of the first Defender Trophy, plus reusable content for recruitment, dealerships, events, press, internal engagement, sponsor activations, heritage storytelling, and purpose-driven environments.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">Why include a healthcare angle?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">Reality Telling recently completed an immersive project built around the Castellers of Catalunya, the human towers where every single person, regardless of size or position, has to hold for the whole structure to stand. It's the same spirit driving Defender Trophy: teamwork, trust, and the idea that everyone in the structure matters. That project found a natural home in nursing and care settings, where residents experienced the height, the tension, and the collective effort of something they could no longer physically do. The same approach could give selected Defender Trophy moments a second life: for people who can't access adventure, nature, or wild landscapes, immersive storytelling offers a sense of movement, presence, and reconnection.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">What's the simplest version?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">One embedded immersive storyteller capturing selected 360° moments during the event, resulting in a short immersive experience and a small library of reusable 360° scenes.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">What's the ideal version?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">A curated immersive Defender Trophy library combining 360° capture, selected stereoscopic scenes, aerial immersive views, still photography, social cutdowns, and a headset-ready app experience.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">What would this cost?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">This isn't being proposed as a one-off paid production job. The goal is a long-term relationship, not a quick fee this year. I'm already part of the Defender Trophy tribe, and the ambition is to take that further: bringing genuine creative and production value to the table, adapting to whatever standard production rates Defender already has in place for a DP or camera operator role. The conversation is about fit first, terms second.</div>
      </details>

      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-question">What's the next step?</summary>
        <div class="faq-answer">A short creative call with the Defender Trophy/Defender production team to understand whether this can fit into the existing production plan and where immersive storytelling could add the most value.</div>
      </details>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

